{"id":"d3cdeb51d01fb81f354b47f459b8c57a2372b702","axis":"silent","repo":"vimeo/psalm","sha":"d3cdeb51d01fb81f354b47f459b8c57a2372b702","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"UPGRADING.md","lines":["@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@"," "," ## Changed"," ","+- [BC] Readers of `dictionaries/CallMap_*.php` must use `$entry[0] ?? $entry[-1]` for the analysis return type: index `0` is omitted when it equals the reflected signature at `-1`. Optional index `-2` is return-signature metadata (`tentative` or `none`), not a parameter type. Only string keys describe parameters. See [the callmap format](docs/contributing/editing_callmaps.md#full-callmap-format)."," - [BC] The `self-accessing-callable`, `self-accessing-Closure`, `self-mutating-callable` and `self-mutating-Closure` types were removed: use `Closure[read-props](...)` and `Closure[read-props|write-this-props|write-refs](...)` (or any other capability set). `pure`, `impure`, `read-props`, `write-this-props`, `write-props`, `read-globals`, `write-globals`, `write-refs`, `io` and `time` are now reserved type names."," - [BC] Capability sets are printed without the `mutation-free` and `external-mutation-free` aliases (`read-props`, `read-props|write-this-props|write-refs`), and `MissingPureAnnotation`, `MissingImmutableAnnotation`, `MissingAbstractPureAnnotation`, `MissingInterfaceImmutableAnnotation` and their `--alter` fixes use `@psalm-capabilities` instead of `@psalm-mutation-free` and `@psalm-external-mutation-free` (`@psalm-pure`, `@psalm-impure`, `@psalm-immutable` and `@psalm-mutable` are still suggested). `@psalm-mutation-free` and `@psalm-external-mutation-free` are still accepted but no longer documented; `mutation-free` and `external-mutation-free` are not capability names (use `read-props` and `read-props|write-this-props|write-refs` in `@psalm-capabilities`, closure types and purity template arguments). `@psalm-capabilities` on a class needing at most `read-props` now specializes taints like `@psalm-pure` and `@psalm-mutation-free` do."," - [BC] Each capability name denotes that capability alone: `write-this-props` and `write-props` no longer include `read-props`, `write-props` no longer includes `write-this-props` (it only allows writing objects other than `$this`), and `write-globals` no longer includes `read-globals`. Write the capabilities out (`read-props|write-this-props`, `read-globals|write-globals`); capability sets are printed the same way, one name per capability. Writes are charged only their write capability: assigning a static property, a superglobal or a `global` variable needs `write-globals` alone (compound assignments and increments also read, and `static` variables need both), and using `$this` needs `read-props` or `write-this-props`, so a setter returning `$this` may be `write-this-props`."],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"bin/stubs/gen_base_callmap.php","lines":["@@ -61,15 +61,23 @@ function typeToString($reflection_type, string $defaultType): string"," function paramsToEntries(ReflectionFunctionAbstract $reflectionFunction, string $defaultReturnType): array"," {","     // phpcs:disable SlevomatCodingStandard.Numbers.RequireNumericLiteralSeparator.RequiredNumericLiteralSeparator","-    $signature = PHP_VERSION_ID >= 80100 ? (","-        $reflectionFunction->getTentativeReturnType() ?? $reflectionFunction->getReturnType()","-    ) : $reflectionFunction->getReturnType();","+    $native = $reflectionFunction->getReturnType();","+    $tentative = PHP_VERSION_ID >= 80100 ? $reflectionFunction->getTentativeReturnType() : null;","+    $signature = $native ?? $tentative;"," ","     $res = [typeToString($signature, $defaultReturnType)];"," ","     // Keep the reflected contract separate from the return type refined by callmap overrides.","     if ($signature !== null) {","         $res = [-1 => typeToString($signature, 'mixed')];","+        if ($native === null) {","+            $res[-2] = 'tentative';","+        }","+    } elseif ($reflectionFunction->isIntern